    "version": 1,
    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that the cluster remains healthy when a worker node (no etcd) fails,\nand that the node can rejoin after being restarted.\n\nTest sequence:\n  1. Confirm 5 nodes heartbeating and cluster healthy (baseline)\n  2. Stop node-4 container (docker stop \u2014 simulates node crash/power loss)\n  3. Assert cluster is still healthy with 4 nodes heartbeating\n  4. Assert etcd quorum is maintained (3 members still active)\n  5. Restart node-4\n  6. Wait for node-4 to rejoin (heartbeat re-appears in etcd)\n  7. Assert 5 nodes heartbeating again\n\nnode-4 is chosen because:\n  - It does NOT run etcd \u2014 stopping it cannot break quorum\n  - It's a worker node \u2014 no critical control-plane services\n  - Stopping it simulates the most common failure mode (node crash)\n\nThis test proves the cluster can survive single-node worker failures without\noperator intervention, and that nodes self-heal on restart.",
